      "text": "The Akashalife (AK1111) on BSC was suspected to have been attacked, resulting in a loss of approximately $31.5K."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "AK1111, a LayerZero OFT token contract on BNB Chain, was exploited on 23 November 2024. The attacker used a permissionless function to freely mint tokens, draining liquidity pools and causing losses of around $31,500. The vulnerable mint function bypassed LayerZero's intended access controls. The contract implemented a public mint-capable function (nonblockingLzReceive1) with no access control, allowing anyone to mint arbitrary amounts of AK1111 tokens outside the intended guarded cross-chain pipeline. This violated the fundamental invariant that new supply can only be created after verified cross-chain burns."
    }
